// field_image_pkg_inherited.vlt -- inherited-warning waivers, scoped BY FILE.
//
// `fpga/rtl/field/generated/zhao_field_host_image_pkg.sv` is S1's generated
// schema package. It declares every ZFH2 offset, length, section kind and
// enumeration, and ANY ONE CONSUMER uses only a fraction of them -- which is
// the point of a single generated source of truth. Linting a consumer at
// `-Wall` therefore reports ~70 UNUSEDPARAM warnings that belong to the
// package's completeness, not to the consumer.
//
// THIS IS THE FIRST THING IN THE TREE TO ELABORATE THAT PACKAGE, and that was
// measured rather than assumed: at the commit this file was written, a
// tree-wide search for `zhao_field_host_image_pkg` matched exactly two files --
// the package itself and `fpga/rtl/field/zhao_field_loader.sv`. S1's roundtrip
// evidence is C++-side; the SystemVerilog half had never been linted or
// elaborated at all.
//
// (That sentence originally began its last line with the simulator's name,
// which made this a BADVLTPRAGMA -- CLAUDE.md's "a comment whose first word
// after `//` is `verilator` is a pragma" trap, caught here on first lint.)
//
// THE SIBLING GENERATED PACKAGE DOES NOT NEED THIS, and the difference is the
// finding: `fpga/rtl/generated/zhao_abi_pkg.sv` carries TWENTY-SEVEN
// `/* verilator lint_off UNUSEDPARAM */` pairs emitted by its own generator.
// `tools/field/gen_field_host_schema.py` emits none -- a search of that file
// for `lint_off` returns nothing. So the right long-term repair is in the
// GENERATOR, matching the established pattern, and it belongs to whoever owns
// the schema. This waiver is the short-term half and it is deliberately
// narrow: one rule, one file.
//
// WHY A .vlt AND NOT `-Wno-UNUSEDPARAM` ON THE COMMAND LINE. A blanket
// suppression would also hide an unused parameter in `zhao_field_loader.sv`
// itself, which is the one file this lint exists to keep clean.
//
// A NOTE ON THE GLOB, inherited from `tests/shell/v3_closure_inherited.vlt`
// and NOT re-derived: Verilator reports Windows paths with MIXED separators,
// so a pattern containing a literal `/` before the basename can match nothing
// -- and a waiver that matches nothing is perfectly silent about being
// useless. `?` matches a single character in Verilator's globs, so the
// separator-agnostic spelling below cannot rot that way.
//
// This is a WAIVER, not a fix.
`verilator_config

lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM -file "*zhao_field_host_image_pkg.sv"
